# CITATION.cff — replace the author placeholders with the real author names
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work (code, data analyses, or manuscript), please cite it as follows."
title: >-
  Multi-environment genomic prediction under genotype × environment
  interaction: a simulation study validated in CIMMYT wheat
authors:
  - name: "charu1231"   # TODO: replace with real given-names / family-names
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
keywords:
  - genomic selection
  - GBLUP
  - genotype by environment interaction
  - multi-trait model
  - reaction norm
  - factor-analytic
  - wheat
  - simulation
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/charu1231/plant-breeding-and-related-works-"
abstract: >-
  A fully reproducible, pure-Python benchmark of multi-environment
  genomic-prediction models (single-environment GBLUP, naive mean,
  reaction-norm, factor-analytic, and multi-trait GBLUP) across a controlled
  GxE gradient, validated on the public CIMMYT wheat panel (Crossa et al. 2010,
  Genetics 186:713-724). Includes the forward population + GxE simulator, the
  analysis pipeline, all results, figures, and a submission-ready manuscript.
